{
  "$comment": "Structured action wire (ADR structured-action-wire): both stacks must read `wire` and `canonical` as the same chain, and the editor must write `canonical` back: the shortest form (ADR extensible-document-kinds W4) — an argument at its declared default is dropped, a primary argument alone is written bare. `names` is the top-level step sequence (an action's wire name, or `if`). Plugin: KeyedStepParser; editor: lib/actions/structuredSteps.ts. Unknown action keys (module Actions, ADR extensible-document-kinds decision 5) are pinned by a later batch.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "arg-less action: null value and bare string are the same step",
      "wire": [
        {
          "close_menu": null
        },
        "open_previous_menu",
        {
          "close_dialog": null
        }
      ],
      "canonical": [
        "close_menu",
        "open_previous_menu",
        "close_dialog"
      ],
      "names": [
        "close_menu",
        "open_previous_menu",
        "close_dialog"
      ]
    },
